WEBVTT

00:00:02.382 --> 00:00:04.993
You know, Guy and I,
we're too different.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:06.995
Well, you and I are different,

00:00:07.169 --> 00:00:09.781
and we get along great, right?

00:00:09.955 --> 00:00:11.870
Yeah, yeah. But it's...

00:00:12.044 --> 00:00:13.175
it's-it's complicated.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.220
He's a boy.

00:00:14.394 --> 00:00:16.918
He is, um...

00:00:17.092 --> 00:00:18.529
stupid.

00:00:18.703 --> 00:00:19.834
You know, it's different.

00:00:20.008 --> 00:00:22.141
What's the matter?
Boy problems?

00:00:22.315 --> 00:00:25.449
Well, in my day,
we didn't have boy problems

00:00:25.623 --> 00:00:27.755
because we didn't have any boys

00:00:27.929 --> 00:00:30.367
or men or clothes.

00:00:30.541 --> 00:00:33.979
We were a warrior tribe
of wimmins.

00:00:34.153 --> 00:00:37.156
The Thunder Sisters.

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:40.377
[gasps]
What's a Thunder Sister?

00:00:40.551 --> 00:00:42.683
Just Gran's old bedtime stories.

00:00:42.857 --> 00:00:46.426
-True stories!
-Okay. Dawn, stop talking

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.515
-to the crazy lady. Whoa!
-[growling]

00:00:48.689 --> 00:00:51.170
We aren't actually gonna
cross that, are we?

00:00:51.344 --> 00:00:52.954
Yes.
Sandy's tracking the scent.

00:00:53.128 --> 00:00:55.392
Well, there's got to be
another way. You know?

00:00:55.566 --> 00:00:57.132
Maybe one that's stable

00:00:57.307 --> 00:00:59.874
and not infested
with land sharks!

00:01:00.048 --> 00:01:01.267
UGGA:
Tell you what,

00:01:01.441 --> 00:01:03.138
you be in charge
of gift baskets,

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:06.098
and I'll be in charge
of tracking the men. We cross.

00:01:06.272 --> 00:01:08.318
-[Gran yelps]
-Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

00:01:08.492 --> 00:01:10.537
-We are not crossing this.
-UGGA: My cat, my rules.

00:01:10.711 --> 00:01:11.886
We cross!

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.019
-Maybe we should take a vote?
-Around!

00:01:14.193 --> 00:01:15.499
[screams]

00:01:15.673 --> 00:01:16.674
-Cross!
-[both screaming]

00:01:16.848 --> 00:01:18.110
Around!

00:01:18.284 --> 00:01:19.372
Cross!

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:21.418
-HOPE: Around!
-[growls]

00:01:24.986 --> 00:01:27.249
-UGGA: Sandy, come!
-[growls, chuckles]

00:01:27.424 --> 00:01:28.686
Thank you, Hope.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.253
This is so much safer.

00:01:31.428 --> 00:01:33.517
[monkeys chittering]

00:01:33.691 --> 00:01:35.519
PHIL:
I can't see!

00:01:35.693 --> 00:01:36.911
What's happening?

00:01:37.085 --> 00:01:38.565
GUY [crying]:
Where are they taking us?

00:01:38.739 --> 00:01:41.089
Hold tight, Guy. As soon
as we get out of this log,

00:01:41.263 --> 00:01:44.136
I'll start swinging and
punching our way to freedom.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:46.399
[screams]

00:01:48.836 --> 00:01:49.881
[Guy groans]

00:01:50.055 --> 00:01:51.796
Come on, punch monkeys!

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:55.277
Let's get this on!

00:01:55.452 --> 00:01:57.279
-[grunts]
-[blows landing]

00:01:57.454 --> 00:01:59.673
Oh! Ow! [grunts]

00:01:59.847 --> 00:02:01.371
[groans]

00:02:01.545 --> 00:02:03.590
It's-it's not
just punch monkeys.

00:02:03.764 --> 00:02:04.852
It's-it's kick monkeys,

00:02:05.026 --> 00:02:06.201
headbutt monkeys,

00:02:06.376 --> 00:02:07.464
low-blow monkeys,

00:02:07.638 --> 00:02:09.509
bite monkeys, ab-tight monkeys!

00:02:09.683 --> 00:02:10.945
Shoulders that punch,

00:02:11.119 --> 00:02:12.338
tails that crunch,

00:02:12.512 --> 00:02:13.470
deranged stranglers,

00:02:13.644 --> 00:02:15.254
strange danglers,
fanged manglers,

00:02:15.428 --> 00:02:16.473
mouth breathers,

00:02:16.647 --> 00:02:17.604
brain squeezers

00:02:17.778 --> 00:02:21.216
and a dude with weird eyes.

00:02:22.217 --> 00:02:23.654
[hums]

00:02:23.828 --> 00:02:24.785
[explosions]

00:02:24.959 --> 00:02:26.961
[shrieking]

00:02:30.182 --> 00:02:31.139
[growls]

00:02:31.313 --> 00:02:33.185
[monkeys chittering]

00:02:38.233 --> 00:02:39.496
[monkeys gasp]

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:42.020
Hmm. They seem to have

00:02:42.194 --> 00:02:43.891
some kind of primitive language.

00:02:44.065 --> 00:02:46.154
Oh, but you can't speak it,
huh, smarty-pants?

00:02:46.328 --> 00:02:47.852
Well, no.

00:02:48.026 --> 00:02:49.897
But I'm sure after
a few months in captivity...

00:02:50.071 --> 00:02:51.246
I can talk to them.

00:02:51.421 --> 00:02:53.118
I'm fluent in punch monkey.

00:02:53.292 --> 00:02:54.598
-You are?
-Impossible.

00:02:54.772 --> 00:02:56.469
GUY: Oh, I really
don't want to do this.

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:57.949
It's not a pretty language.

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:00.212
[clears throat]

00:03:00.386 --> 00:03:02.954
Pardon me. I'd like to ask...

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:06.131
Hmm.

00:03:06.305 --> 00:03:07.915
-[grunts] Uh-huh.
-[chittering]

00:03:08.089 --> 00:03:10.352
-[grunts] I see.
-GRUG: So, what's he saying?

00:03:10.527 --> 00:03:12.572
[grunts] They're angry

00:03:12.746 --> 00:03:15.793
-because Phil broke the terms
of their contract. -Ludicrous!

00:03:15.967 --> 00:03:17.882
We had no formal agreement,
you chiselers.

00:03:18.056 --> 00:03:20.841
[grunts]
Also, they want their bananas.

00:03:21.015 --> 00:03:23.148
Yeah, bananas are delicious.

00:03:23.322 --> 00:03:25.324
Why is that our problem?

00:03:25.498 --> 00:03:27.413
And one more question.

00:03:27.587 --> 00:03:29.459
[whimpers]

00:03:29.633 --> 00:03:31.112
[cracks knuckles]

00:03:31.286 --> 00:03:32.853
[shrieks]
Many moons ago...

00:03:33.027 --> 00:03:34.638
[grunts]
their world was a paradise.

00:03:34.812 --> 00:03:37.641
[grunts] Oh, this is
gonna be a long story.

00:03:37.815 --> 00:03:40.165
"It was a time of much joy.

00:03:40.339 --> 00:03:42.341
"The water flowed freely.

00:03:42.515 --> 00:03:44.648
-The bananas grew in bunches."
-[laughs]

00:03:44.822 --> 00:03:46.040
-"We had art..."
-ALL: Oh!

00:03:46.214 --> 00:03:47.433
-"...politics..."
-[both shrieking]

00:03:47.607 --> 00:03:49.522
-"...economics..."
-BOTH: Oh.

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:51.611
"...but most of all, bananas.

00:03:51.785 --> 00:03:53.570
"So many bananas.

00:03:53.744 --> 00:03:55.615
"Then, at full moon,

00:03:55.789 --> 00:03:58.792
-the monster came
for its bananas."-[growls]

00:03:58.966 --> 00:04:00.664
-[chuckles]: "Yep. Good times."
-GRUG: Wait.

00:04:00.838 --> 00:04:03.449
-Um, go back.
-Yeah, did he say "monster"?

00:04:03.623 --> 00:04:06.365
We are not going back!
As I was saying,

00:04:06.539 --> 00:04:07.671
"Good times.

00:04:07.845 --> 00:04:09.977
"But then,
for some strange reason,

00:04:10.151 --> 00:04:11.675
"the water went away.

00:04:11.849 --> 00:04:14.982
"After that,
the bananas went away, too.

00:04:15.156 --> 00:04:17.332
"But the monster
didn't go away. No.

00:04:17.507 --> 00:04:20.553
-It came back for its bananas."
-[growling]

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:22.033
"There were no bananas."

00:04:22.207 --> 00:04:24.949
[monkeys shrieking]

00:04:28.779 --> 00:04:32.347
In summary,
they really need those bananas.

00:04:32.522 --> 00:04:34.524
Monsters, bananas.

00:04:34.698 --> 00:04:36.700
I'll tell you
what their problem is.

00:04:36.874 --> 00:04:38.919
Their water supply is dried-up.

00:04:39.093 --> 00:04:41.052
Tell them this
word for word, Guy.

00:04:41.226 --> 00:04:44.011
I, Phil Betterman,
single-handedly turned a desert

00:04:44.185 --> 00:04:47.928
into an oasis by diverting water
from a high mountain source,

00:04:48.102 --> 00:04:50.365
much like that one.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.106
Wait, Guy, don't translate that.

00:04:54.065 --> 00:04:55.588
-[monkeys gasp]
-[inhales sharply] Too late?

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:57.634
[monkeys shrieking]

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.419
It was all him.

00:05:00.593 --> 00:05:02.508
He stole your water,
ate your bananas

00:05:02.682 --> 00:05:03.640
and ruined your society.

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:06.033
-[chuckles]
-That's it!

00:05:06.207 --> 00:05:08.209
I will not be pelted!

00:05:09.341 --> 00:05:12.039
Now, impertinent apes,

00:05:12.213 --> 00:05:14.389
meet the full force
of my intellect.

00:05:14.564 --> 00:05:17.044
Look upon
Betterman the toolmaker

00:05:17.218 --> 00:05:18.959
and despair.

00:05:19.133 --> 00:05:20.744
-Jab, jab.
-[monkeys screech]

00:05:20.918 --> 00:05:22.223
MONKEYS:
Oh.

00:05:22.397 --> 00:05:24.399
[monkeys grunting]

00:05:24.574 --> 00:05:26.967
♪ ♪

00:05:30.623 --> 00:05:33.974
-[chanting rhythmically]
-Way to go, Phil.

00:05:34.148 --> 00:05:35.933
Way to go, Hope.

00:05:36.107 --> 00:05:38.022
We lost the scent.

00:05:39.545 --> 00:05:40.807
[whimpers]

00:05:40.981 --> 00:05:42.896
No, no, no, no, no, no!

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:45.290
Travel window!
Come on, come on.

00:05:45.464 --> 00:05:47.640
Whew!
It still works, everybody.

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:50.382
We are... lost.

00:05:50.556 --> 00:05:52.514
This is why you
don't follow cave people.

00:05:52.689 --> 00:05:54.255
One more word out of...

00:05:54.429 --> 00:05:58.346
We have forgotten the old ways,

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:00.131
the ways of the world
when it was young

00:06:00.305 --> 00:06:01.741
and I was young,

00:06:01.915 --> 00:06:04.788
when I was the queen matriarch

00:06:04.962 --> 00:06:08.835
of a warrior tribe of wimmins!

00:06:09.009 --> 00:06:10.445
The Thunder Sisters.

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:11.795
You got it, girl.

00:06:11.969 --> 00:06:13.797
The Thunder Sisters!

00:06:13.971 --> 00:06:15.755
We faced down danger

00:06:15.929 --> 00:06:17.975
and kicked death in the crotch!

00:06:18.149 --> 00:06:19.585
We don't need
the Thunder Sisters, Mom.

00:06:19.759 --> 00:06:21.935
We need a way to find the men.

00:06:22.109 --> 00:06:23.807
Oh, a way?

00:06:23.981 --> 00:06:26.984
The Thunder Sisters
always find a way!

00:06:27.158 --> 00:06:29.421
Think you got one more flight
in you, old girl?

00:06:29.595 --> 00:06:30.640
[caws]

00:06:31.641 --> 00:06:33.817
Oh, my goodness.

